TITLE:: Audrey
summary:: a feedback synth engine, modelling electric guitar feedback
categories:: UGens>Generators>PhysicalModels

DESCRIPTION::
Audrey is based on the open source project Audrey II link::https://www.synthux.academy/store/audrey-ii:: by Synthux Academy link:: https://www.synthux.academy/::. It consists of a Karplus-Strong string model excited by some constant very low white noise signal, an overdrive/clipping stage, an EQ (HP/LP) and a reverb section, which feeds back via a delay line into the string model. There's an additional delay/echo section for looping or echo duties. The design was inspired by the sound and the physics of an electric guitar feeding back with a cranked up amp.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
(describe method here)

ARGUMENT:: in1
audio input left

ARGUMENT:: in2
audio input right

ARGUMENT:: freq
fundamental frequency of the string model in Hz

ARGUMENT:: fb_gain
feedback gain (0..1)

ARGUMENT:: body
delay time parameter (0..1)

ARGUMENT:: hp
Highpass cutoff filter frequency of the EQ section in Hz

ARGUMENT:: lp
Lowpass cutoff filter frequency of the EQ section in Hz

ARGUMENT:: drywet
Dry/wet level of reverb section

ARGUMENT:: decay
decay rate of the reverb section, default=0.8, range=(0..1)

ARGUMENT:: drive
drive amount, default=0.4, range=(0..1)

ARGUMENT:: echo_send
send amount of the echo section, default=0.1, range=(0..1)

ARGUMENT:: echo_time
echo/delay time of the echo section, default=0.5, range=(0..1)

ARGUMENT:: echo_fb
feedback amount of the echo section, default=0.5, range=(0..1)



EXAMPLES::

code::
// wait a bit...
{ Audrey.ar() }.play

{ Audrey.ar(freq: 50, fb_gain: 0.65, body: LFNoise1.kr(0.1).range(0.2,0.4)) }.play

(
{
	var freq = LFNoise0.kr(0.13).range(10, 90).midicps;
	var body = LFNoise1.kr(0.1).range(0,1);
	Audrey.ar(freq: freq, fb_gain: 0.45, body: body, lp: 5000, drywet: 0.4, drive: 0.6);
}.play
)

// echo stuff ...
(
{
	var gain = LFNoise1.kr(0.3).range(0.5, 0.7);
	var trigger = Dust.kr( LFNoise2.kr(0.1).range(0.1, 7) );
	var time = TRand.kr(trig: trigger);

	Audrey.ar(freq: 33, fb_gain: gain, body: 0.1,
		echo_send: 0.7,
		echo_time: time,
		echo_fb: 0.95);
}.play
)
::
